{"created": "2026-11-05T22:55:47.668349+00:00", "modified": "2026-11-05T23:02:42.203348+00:00", "id": 23990857, "conceptrecid": "22965031", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23990857", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22965031", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23990857", "metadata": {"title": "Axes and Level Sets of a Jacquard Pattern System \u2014 two companion notes", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23990857", "publication_date": "2026-11-05", "description": "<p class=\"FirstParagraph\">Two companion notes on a Jacquard axis grammar. The original axis notes are kept in axes-notes-originales/. The expanded Chladni note, version 2.15, is titled &ldquo;From a Jacquard Axis Grammar to Eigenmodes: Chebyshev Cycles, Cyclotomic Condensation, and a Complete Period-N Spectral Classification&rdquo;. Version 2.14 is kept in manuscrit-v2.14/.</p>\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\">Version 2.15 extends Section 4.26 and adds Section 4.27: - the finite recognition of a class from its radial weights, established at side twelve, does not extend to larger orders: at source order 18 there are 128 pairs with equal radial weights, and at order 30 a balanced pair with equal moduli at every index; - four levels of information are kept apart: signed coefficients, moduli, radial weights and radial support; - area profiles as a complementary geometric selection, with the open question of the factor sixteen in the count 379,920; - a computed sonification of a family of 256 patterns at order 18, with a self-contained keyboard page and a prototype page in which the sound selects a pattern.</p>\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\">The spectral counts concern finite corpora. The sonifications are computations, not physical measurements. Spectral injectivity beyond side twelve and any measurement on a plate remain open. The record includes editable sources, code, data and verification logs.</p>\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\">Licence: texts and figures under CC BY 4.0; code under AGPL v3.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{